From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vikash Garodia <vikash.garodia@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:19:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] media: iris: wait for vpu NoC to enter low power during
 power off

The recommended hardware sequence requires software to wait for vpu NoC
to enter in low power mode and then deassert the low power idle (LPI)
control. Add the missing LPI status poll and move the LPI control
deassertion after the hardware acks LPI mode. This avoids any pending
transactions on vpu NoC before shutting it down.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261001-kaanapali-iris-v4-1-642f9ac5e699@oss.qualcomm.com
Fixes: dde659d37036 ("media: iris: Introduce vpu ops for vpu4 with necessary hooks")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Co-developed-by: Vishnu Reddy <busanna.reddy@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Vishnu Reddy <busanna.reddy@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Vikash Garodia <vikash.garodia@oss.qualcomm.com>

[ from qualcomm-linux/kernel-topics tech/mm/video 85845a0a4cbd (FROMLIST, v4 1/6 of "media: iris: add support
  for kaanapali platform"); ported to the iceland iris_vpu4x.c, which already deasserts the LPI control
  after the handshake loop: only the LPI status poll is added in front of that write ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu4x.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu4x.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu4x.c
index ca9bb8710685..131a86ddd8e8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu4x.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu4x.c
@@ -318,6 +318,8 @@ static void iris_vpu4x_power_off_hardware(struct iris_core *core)
 	if (!handshake_done && handshake_busy)
 		dev_err(core->dev, "LPI handshake timeout\n");
 
+	readl_poll_timeout(core->reg_base + AON_WRAPPER_MVP_NOC_LPI_STATUS,
+			   value, value & BIT(0), 200, 2000);
 	writel(0x0, core->reg_base + AON_WRAPPER_MVP_NOC_LPI_CONTROL);
 
 	writel(MVP_NOC_RESET_REQ_MASK, core->reg_base + AON_WRAPPER_MVP_NOC_RESET_REQ);
